A||||5||My7Fieros||WHAT? BAD GASOLINE WAS THE PROBLEM ALL THIS TIME?!!!!||||4||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-08-2001||09:20 PM||||You know, for almost the past year I havent driven my Formula because it wasn't acting right. It was suffering from an intermitten miss...(poot poot very noticably, tach jumping wildly) so I stopped driving it. This started last Christmas...I remember putting some gas in it on Christmas day and it started all that crap that night. So I parked it and started driving the other Fieros. Well over the past almost year (and countless posts) I'd start it up, let it run, maybe drive it around the block a couple of times, all the while fearful of it stalling (which it did sometimes) and of course watching and hearing the "poot poot".<BR>Well the long short of it (I know, too late) is that Im trading it in a few days for an Indy that Im gonna restore....<BR><B>But</B>, get this. After a year of periodically starting and buzzing around the block Ive burned all the gas in it (from last Christmas). So I go the other night and filled it up w/gas (93)...IT HAS NOT HAD A SINGLE PROBLEM SINCE AND HAS RUN PERFECTLY! Ive started driving it again the past few days...Bad gasoline? Could this have been the problem? It feels great to drive it again, especially since its an automatic! All my other Fieros (and my Mustang) are manuals......and it figures cause now Im gonna trade it! Oh well, I want the Indy pretty bad so I guess its ok. Just wish I knew this a year ago!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <BR>(BTW Im trading w/ Pennocks "NDFieroTN".<BR>Has anyone else ever had a similar prob?<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Pheagey||10-08-2001||09:33 PM||||My7Fieros, dude i so feel your pain. I rove down the Miami to visit family for the weekend and on the way up I filled it up. The entire time back it slowly started to loss a lil power and 'cought' as I drove at aroun 65-70. The more i drove it around town (to work, etc) the more irritating ti would be; I'd tey to jump off the line at a red and brrrurmmmr poob nnenennerrrrrr I would go. After burning gas buy running in high RPM's for about a week and running fuel system cleaner, new fuel filter, and new (cheap) plugs I finally ran out of gas. <BR>The new gas fixd it right up! D@mn Miami gass....<BR>It still misse donce in a while but I attribute that to needing  other small stuff like good plugwire and a Supercharger &lt;smerk&gt;.<BR>Anyways, moral of the story: If at 1st you cann't fix it, run it till it dies &lt;do fiero's ever die?&gt;.<BR> <A HREF="Http://www.Lithiumeffects.com/car.html" TARGET=_blank>Http://www.Lithiumeffects.com/car.html</A> <BR>Pheagey's Fiero site comming soon!||||reg||10
Z||000002||terryk||10-08-2001||09:34 PM||||Maybe you had a stuck injector? Very annoying.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||10-08-2001||09:42 PM||||I had that happen with a Pinto when I was in college.  I rebuilt the carb, tuned it up, changed filters, checked timing and nothing.  Finally just ran the bad gas out and it cleared up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||10-08-2001||09:50 PM||||Yeah, it happens.  You might want to drain that sucker -- you may still have a little water in the bottom of the tank.<BR>||||reg||1
